/2410.13965v1\",\n+    \"scope\": \"Definitions and Theorems1-2; Section8.2 p31 eq8.3; Section8.4; relevant pages read and p31 rendered\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"7fa62d5ecbb692a1bcbfc486816c6beccee5fbe66353f2f64355f0e43b2f5178\",\n+    \"bytes\": 546706\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"name\": \"schwarz2010.pdf\",\n+    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1001.1805\",\n+    \"scope\": \"Supplementary boundary-Schwarz context only, not the source of the resolution\",\n+    \"sha256\": \"6b03858a6a4c5bce688048e3dec5567006ad6802d9be8e1371a25320ea67f4d0\",\n+    \"bytes\": 180394\n+  }\n+]"},{"sha":"cca1968057b20500921dd1e00f47e9dc589f87bd","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30000703/source_record.json","status":"added","additions":72,"deletions":0,"changes":72,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fsource_record.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fsource_record.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fsource_record.json?ref=036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+{\n+  \"id\": 30000703,\n+  \"problem_number\": \"OWR-1460-009\",\n+  \"title\": \"Boundary Behavior under Asymptotic Schwarz\\u2013Pick Equality\",\n+  \"statement\": \"Let $f:\\\\mathbb{D}\\\\to\\\\mathbb{D}$ be holomorphic and suppose $\\\\lim_{z\\\\to1}(1-|z|^2)|f'(z)|/(1-|f(z)|^2)=1$. What can be said about the boundary behavior of $f$ at $z=1$?\",\n+  \"background\": \"Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\\n\\n**Source report:** [Normal Families and Complex Dynamics (2007), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/09, pp. 487--548](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/09)\\n\\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-21)\\n\\n**Status:** partially solved\\n\\n**Assessment.** The condition is governed by boundary Schwarz--Pick and Julia--Caratheodory theory, which gives strong angular boundary conclusions and rigidity in extremal cases. A complete unrestricted description for every approach to the boundary point is not supplied by the standard theorem.\\n\\n**Sources checked.**\\n\\n- [original problem report](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/09)\\n- [Schwarz lemma at the boundary](https://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1805)\\n- [hyperbolic distortion at the boundary](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.13965)\\n\\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.\",\n+  \"difficulty_level_id\": 3,\n+  \"status\": \"partially_solved\",\n+  \"proposed_by\": null,\n+  \"proposed_year\": 2007,\n+  \"category_id\": 11,\n+  \"set_id\": 15,\n+  \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/09\",\n+  \"source_citation\": \"Normal Families and Complex Dynamics (2007), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2007/09, pp. 487--548\",\n+  \"literature_assessment\": \"The condition is governed by boundary Schwarz--Pick and Julia--Caratheodory theory, which gives strong angular boundary conclusions and rigidity in extremal cases. A complete unrestricted description for every approach to the boundary point is not supplied by the standard theorem.\",\n+  \"literature_sources\": [\n+    {\n+      \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2007/09\",\n+      \"label\": \"original problem report\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1805\",\n+      \"label\": \"Schwarz lemma at the boundary\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.13965\",\n+      \"label\": \"hyperbolic distortion at the boundary\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"literature_checked_at\": \"2026-08-21\",\n+  \"tags\": [\n+    \"owr\",\n+    \"oberwolfach-reports\",\n+    \"OWR-1460-009\",\n+    \"literature-status:partially-solved\",\n+    \"owr-year:2007\"\n+  ],\n+  \"view_count\": 0,\n+  \"favorite_count\": 0,\n+  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-25T00:00:00Z\",\n+  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-16T12:06:53Z\",\n+  \"published\": true,\n+  \"category\": {\n+    \"id\": 11,\n+    \"name\": \"dynamical_systems\",\n+    \"display_name\": \"Dynamical Systems\",\n+    \"description\": \"Problems about long-term behavior of deterministic systems, Hamiltonian dynamics, and periodic orbits.\",\n+    \"slug\": \"dynamical-systems\",\n+    \"order_index\": 11,\n+    \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T15:26:25.671Z\"\n+  },\n+  \"difficulty\": {\n+    \"id\": 3,\n+    \"level\": 3,\n+    \"name\": \"L3: Advanced\",\n+    \"description\": \"Difficult problems requiring specialized knowledge and sophisticated techniques.\",\n+    \"color_class\": \"text-yellow-600 bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-200\"\n+  },\n+  \"set\": {\n+    \"id\": 15,\n+    \"name\": \"oberwolfach_reports_open_problems\",\n+    \"display_name\": \"Oberwolfach Reports Open Problems\",\n+    \"description\": \"Open and partially solved problems extracted from Oberwolfach Reports workshop discussions, with report provenance and dated literature assessments.\",\n+    \"slug\": \"oberwolfach-reports-open-problems\",\n+    \"order_index\": 15,\n+    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-25T00:00:00Z\"\n+  },\n+  \"original_statement\": \"Let f: \\ud835\\udd3b\\u2192\\ud835\\udd3b be holomorphic and suppose lim_{z\\u21921} (1\\u2212|z|\\u00b2)|f\\u2032(z)|/(1\\u2212|f(z)|\\u00b2)=1. What can be said about the boundary behavior of f at z=1?\",\n+  \"clean_statement\": \"Let $f:\\\\mathbb{D}\\\\to\\\\mathbb{D}$ be holomorphic and suppose $\\\\lim_{z\\\\to1}(1-|z|^2)|f'(z)|/(1-|f(z)|^2)=1$. What can be said about the boundary behavior of $f$ at $z=1$?\",\n+  \"statement_status\": \"corrected_verified\",\n+  \"statement_verification\": \"The boundary-behavior question is complete; the disk, map, derivative, and limit notation are restored.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"189a3cb257398781098d75c93686ed663667d2ca","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30000703/turns.json","status":"added","additions":6,"deletions":0,"changes":6,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fturns.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fturns.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fturns.json?ref=036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+{\n+  \"id\": 30000703,\n+  \"count\": 0,\n+  \"substantive_attempts\": [],\n+  \"reason\": \"Stopped at known-result source gate; the short point-to-arc application and examples verify the existing criterion rather than constitute a fresh proof-search route.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"52a2ed53ca3e67fa59adb2c30e90afc111a92c81","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30000703/verification.json","status":"added","additions":77,"deletions":0,"changes":77,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fverification.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fverification.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fverification.json?ref=036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@\n+{\n+  \"passed\": 69,\n+  \"failed\": 0,\n+  \"sympy_version\": \"1.14.0\",\n+  \"checks\": {\n+    \"cayley_real_part\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"cayley_derivative\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"exponential_distortion\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"exponential_limit\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"square_distortion\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"square_limit\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"square_deficit\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_1_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_1_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_1_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_2_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_2_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_2_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_3_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_3_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_3_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_4_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_4_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_4_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_5_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_5_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_5_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_6_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_6_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_6_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_7_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_7_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_7_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_8_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_8_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_8_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_9_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_9_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_9_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_10_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_10_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_10_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_11_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_11_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_11_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_12_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_12_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_12_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_13_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_13_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_13_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_14_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_14_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_14_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_15_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_15_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_15_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_16_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_16_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_16_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_17_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_17_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_17_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_18_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_18_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_18_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_19_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_19_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_19_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_20_1/4\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_20_1/3\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"arc_margin_20_2/5\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"example_boundary_value\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"example_derivative\": \"PASS\"\n+  },\n+  \"scope\": \"Exact formula and quantifier-margin controls; the published reflection theorem is an imported analytic result, not a computed claim.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"4d3042e2ce7b5870e9c860c771188d84dafc8706","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30000703/verify.py","status":"added","additions":32,"deletions":0,"changes":32,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fverify.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fverify.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30000703%2Fverify.py?ref=036a5ed59bee5ed79f08349290481584610f1456","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Exact diagnostic identities; no numerical certificate for reflection theorems.\"\"\"\n+from pathlib import Path\n+import json\n+import sympy as s\n+x,y,r,u=s.symbols('x y r u',real=True)\n+z=x+s.I*y\n+checks={}\n+def ck(n,v):\n+ assert bool(v),n\n+ checks[n]='PASS'\n+w=(1-z)/(1+z)\n+ck('cayley_real_part',s.factor(s.re(w)-(1-x*x-y*y)/((1+x)**2+y*y))==0)\n+ck('cayley_derivative',s.cancel(s.diff((1-s.Symbol('z'))/(1+s.Symbol('z')),s.Symbol('z'))+2/(1+s.Symbol('z'))**2)==0)\n+ck('exponential_distortion',s.cancel((2*u*s.exp(-u)/(1-s.exp(-2*u))-u/s.sinh(u)).rewrite(s.exp))==0)\n+ck('exponential_limit',s.limit(u/s.sinh(u),u,0)==1)\n+ck('square_distortion',s.cancel((1-r*r)*2*r/(1-r**4)-2*r/(1+r*r))==0)\n+ck('square_limit',s.limit(2*r/(1+r*r),r,1)==1)\n+ck('square_deficit',s.factor(1-2*r/(1+r*r)-(1-r)**2/(1+r*r))==0)\n+# Triangle estimate behind the point-to-arc argument, checked with exact radii.\n+for j in range(1,21):\n+ delta=s.Rational(1,j)\n+ for a in (s.Rational(1,4),s.Rational(1,3),s.Rational(2,5)):\n+  # |xi-1| <= a*delta, |z-xi| < delta/2 imply |z-1| < delta.\n+  ck(f'arc_margin_{j}_{a}',a*delta+delta/2<delta)\n+q=s.symbols('q')\n+f=s.exp(-(1-q)/(1+q))\n+ck('example_boundary_value',f.subs(q,1)==1)\n+ck('example_derivative',s.diff(f,q).subs(q,1)==s.Rational(1,2))\n+out={'passed':len(checks),'failed':0,'sympy_version':s.__version__,'checks':checks,'scope':'Exact formula and quantifier-margin controls; the published reflection theorem is an imported analytic result, not a computed claim.'}\n+Path(__file__).with_name('verification.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2)+'\\n')\n+print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in out.items() if k!='checks'},indent=2))"}]]